WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.222
Day 9. Sentences, and a story.

2
00:00:02.672 --> 00:00:09.484
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:09.984 --> 00:00:17.750
In the sentences and the story the long words have no dashed line. Your child finds the split in their head, or with a finger.

4
00:00:23.674 --> 00:00:24.913
The word is basket.

5
00:00:25.813 --> 00:00:30.369
The words to say to your child are in the yellow box at the top. Read them out.

6
00:00:30.819 --> 00:00:33.011
Read the six words of job one together.

7
00:00:33.461 --> 00:00:37.493
If a word goes wrong, do not say it. Say the same words every time.

8
00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:42.671
Cover the second beat with a finger. Read the first one. Then uncover the rest.

9
00:00:43.471 --> 00:00:48.231
Then your child reads the three sentences of job two alone, pointing to each word.

10
00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:53.540
There are three small words you tell your child. They are in the grown-up pages at the front.

11
00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:59.000
Then turn to the story. Let your child read it to you, then to someone else in the family.

12
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.145
The pictures are at the bottom, for after the reading.
